--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- chain in MoorDyn-C file kinematics (WaveKin 7 waves, Currents 1 current), 120 s
-- Same held-fairlead studless chain as dynamic_chain_waves.dat (50 m depth), with the water
-- kinematics read from MoorDyn-C's fixed-name files in this folder. WaveKin 7 reads
-- wave_frequencies.txt: `omega Re Im beta` rows (rad/s, m, m, rad), the first at omega = 0; here
-- nine components 0.45-1.25 rad/s of a JONSWAP sea (Hs = 2.5 m, Tp = 9 s), all travelling along
-- +X (beta = 0). Currents 1 reads current_profile.txt: `z ux uy uz` rows after its header rows,
-- here 0.2 m/s at the seabed rising to 0.6 m/s at the surface along +X. CableDyn evaluates the
-- components and the profile exactly at every node (MoorDyn-C's water_grid.txt is not needed).
-- The WaterKin row carries the MoorDyn-C mode (WaterKin and WaveKin are one keyword), and the
-- waves and current rows stay none: a second wave or current source is rejected as double counting.
